{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-892a7e04-b25d-41d1-9762-b9c68f27de5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6c089444fd756b1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-07_6of8m/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E001.md","content":"# Validate EvalHub Server mid-run status data availability\n\n## Description\n\nResolve the two open questions from the strategy that gate the EvalHub UI progress-visibility work: (a) whether the EvalHub Server detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populates `status.benchmarks[]` with per-benchmark status entries while an evaluation job is still running, or only after completion; and (b) what values `status.message.message_code` takes for pre-start failures (admission errors, resource quota, scheduling failures) versus runtime failures, and whether those values are reliably distinguishable. The answers determine whether mid-run benchmark-level progress display and the pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction can be built as specified, or whether the defined fallbacks must be used.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the EvalHub Server source code (upstream `opendatahub-io/eval-hub`) status-reporting paths: where per-benchmark status entries, `started_at`/`completed_at` timestamps, and message codes are written, and whether they are updated during job execution (for example by a runtime watcher) or only at completion.\n- Cross-check findings against the published API reference for `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}` and `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs`.\n- Where feasible, confirm empirically by running an evaluation job against a development instance and inspecting detail-endpoint responses while the job is in progress.\n- Enumerate the `message_code` values (or equivalent fields) emitted on admission/scheduling/resource-quota failure paths versus runtime failure paths, and assess whether the UI can reliably distinguish them.\n- Publish the findings with a per-question go/no-go and the recommended fallback for each dependent UI feature (mid-run benchmark progress display; pre-start failure distinction).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented answer, with evidence (source-code references and/or observed API responses), to whether `status.benchmarks[]` contains per-benchmark status entries while a job is running, or only after completion.\n- A documented enumeration of `status.message.message_code` values for pre-start failure paths versus runtime failure paths, with a determination of whether they are reliably distinguishable.\n- Findings delivered to the ODH Dashboard team with a clear go/no-go per dependent UI feature and a recommended fallback where the answer is negative.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs — de-risks feasibility of mid-run X/N progress and elapsed-time data\n- [P1] Elapsed time display for running jobs — confirms availability of per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps mid-run\n- [P2] Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction — determines whether `message_code` supports the distinction\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50529,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9bfc823f6c83078","agent_id":"a4cf8ceb1799e5d5b","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"2ffbcdb7-cf8a-45c3-a7e9-652d7d7b2481","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:07:40.207Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
