{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cb2160d6-29f4-4843-8cf9-1d8e1cda6489","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c51050f2c6ea3cd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-07_6of8m/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E003.md","content":"# Evaluation job state differentiation in the Evaluations table\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver visually distinct state treatments for evaluation jobs in the Evaluations landing page table, derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` field (available for all jobs without detail fetching): queued/pending, running, failed, and completed, each with a distinct PatternFly icon, color, and label. Includes the pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available, with a graceful fallback to a single \"Failed\" state when the message code is ambiguous or absent. State badges update automatically as the existing list-endpoint polling refreshes, without manual browser refresh.\n\n## Scope\n\n- State mapping from the list endpoint's `status.state`: pending → \"Queued\"; active execution → \"Running\"; failure → \"Failed\" (with `status.message` providing error context); completed → \"Completed\".\n- Distinct PatternFly Label/Icon/color treatment per state, visually distinguishable from one another per the PatternFly status pattern.\n- Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available: when the message indicates an admission error, scheduling failure, or resource constraint, render \"Failed (not started)\"; runtime errors render \"Failed\". When `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, fall back to a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text displayed as supplementary detail.\n- Auto-updating state badge driven by the existing 30-second list polling (state transitions visible without manual page refresh).\n- UX/design review of the state icon and color specifications for PatternFly alignment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job is queued/pending (not yet started), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct \"Queued\" label and visual treatment distinguishable from \"Running\" and \"Failed\" states, measured by distinct icon, color, and label text per the PatternFly status pattern.\n- Given an evaluation job transitions from running to complete, when the user is on the Evaluations landing page without manually refreshing the browser, then the status update is visible within the list endpoint's polling interval (30 seconds), measured by the job row's state label updating automatically.\n- Given an evaluation job failed before execution started (e.g., admission error indicated by `status.message.message_code`), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a treatment that differentiates it from a job that ran and then failed, measured by a label reflecting the failure type and an icon/color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n- Given `status.message.message_code` is ambiguous or absent for a failed job, then the row renders the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n- State icon and color specifications are reviewed and approved by UX/design for PatternFly alignment.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Visual distinction between queued/pending, actively running, failed, and completed states with distinct labels, icons, and color treatments\n- [P0] Auto-refresh mechanism for the Evaluations landing page job list — visible top-level state transitions without manual refresh\n- [P2] Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52505,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9