{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8643fca4-d52f-4f88-913e-53542a0b5f59","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a12f3e5bd3dfafbf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-07_6of8m/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E004.md","content":"# Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver the progress display for running evaluation jobs in the Evaluations landing page table, using the per-job detail data obtained through the detail-polling capability: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps. Elapsed time serves as the primary progress indicator for jobs with few benchmarks (a single-benchmark job shows only 0/N or N/N), with the benchmark count supplementary. Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Benchmark progress display: for a job with N benchmarks, render \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"` from the detail endpoint response.\n- Elapsed time display: computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks, falling back to `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started; formatted for readability (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\").\n- Initial-state behavior: until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, display only the top-level state from the list endpoint (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n- Elapsed time as the primary progress indicator for single-benchmark/few-benchmark jobs, with benchmark count supplementary (mitigation for coarse progress granularity).\n- UX/design review of the progress indicator pattern.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail endpoint response.\n- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response (or `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started).\n- Given no detail fetch has yet returned for a running job, then the row displays only the top-level state from the list endpoint, with no benchmark progress or elapsed time shown.\n- Given a single-benchmark running job, then elapsed time is presented as the primary progress indicator for that row.\n- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed and approved by UX/design.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Auto-refresh mechanism for the Evaluations landing page job list — in-progress job progress made visible\n- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` (display portion)\n- [P1] Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":53362,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9bfc823f6c83078","agent_id":"a4cf8ceb1799e5d5b","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"5f755a8e-d505-43c8-ab15-d6bf496733c6","timestamp":"2026-10-22