{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4139202dd638c4e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n3\ttitle: Detail-polling engine for in-progress evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the detail endpoint's status data is static while a job is\n15\t    running, reduce the polling layer to post-completion refresh and source elapsed\n16\t    time from the list endpoint's resource.created_at; per the strategy risk mitigation,\n17\t    elapsed time becomes the primary progress indicator.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 7\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Detail-polling engine for in-progress evaluation jobs\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDeliver the new detail-polling layer inside the eval-hub-ui dashboard plugin: a React Query based polling capability that identifies the non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed Evaluations table page and fetches their detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) on a 10-second cycle with at most 5 concurrent requests dispatched in round-robin. It adopts the retry-with-exponential-backoff error pattern established by the autorag package, pauses while the browser tab is backgrounded (Page Visibility API), and shows a non-blocking warning when updates are temporarily unavailable. The existing 30-second list-endpoint polling continues unchanged as the first layer. This epic also verifies that the odh-dashboard BFF proxy chain transparently passes detail-endpoint response fields through to the frontend (no code change expected — validation of existing behavior).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- A new detail-polling hook, alongside the existing list fetching in `useEvaluationJobs` / `k8s.ts`, that derives the set of in-progress jobs visible on the current table page (client-side pagination: default 20 rows, options 5/10/20) and polls their detail endpoints.\n44\t- 10-second polling cycle; when all detail fetches for the current page complete, a 10-second timer starts before the next cycle.\n45\t- Concurrency control: at most 5 simultaneous detail requests, dispatched round-robin — as one request completes, the next pending visible in-progress job is fetched, until all have been updated.\n46\t- Page-targeting: changing the table page immediately retargets polling to the newly visible jobs; jobs not in view are not polled.\n47\t- Error handling per the autorag `usePipelineRunQuery` pattern: `placeholderData` preserving the last successful response during transient errors; exponential backoff (`RETRY_DELAY_MS * 2^attempt + jitter`) up to `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`; 4xx errors treated as non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried; a non-blocking inline PatternFly warning Alert shown while status updates are temporarily unavailable; the round-robin continues with the next job when a single request fails (partial progress data is acceptable).\n48\t- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded and one polling cycle triggers immediately when the tab regains focus.\n49\t- Verification that the odh-dashboard BFF proxy path (kube-rbac-proxy → dashboard backend → eval-hub-ui plugin backend → EvalHub Server) transparently passes all detail-endpoint response fields, including `status.benchmarks[]` and per-benchmark timestamps, without filtering.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given more than 5 in-progress jobs on the currently displayed table page, when the detail-polling cycle runs, then at most 5 concurrent detail requests are in flight at any moment and remaining jobs are fetched round-robin as earlier requests complete, measured by observing request concurrency in browser developer tools.\n54\t- Given the user turns to another table page, when detail polling runs, then only jobs visible on the new page are polled and no requests are made for out-of-view jobs.\n55\t- Given the EvalHub Server is temporarily unreachable during detail polling (5xx or network error on a detail fetch), then the last successfully fetched data for the affected job remains displayed, a non-blocking inline warning is shown, the failed request retries with exponential backoff (up to the configured maximum attempts), and the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job, measured by the warning Alert being visible and stale-but-rendered detail data.\n56\t- Given a 4xx response on a detail fetch, then the request is not retried with backoff.\n57\t- Given the user navigates away from the browser tab, when the tab loses focus, then detail polling pauses and no requests are made to the detail endpoint until the tab regains focus, at which point a single polling cycle triggers immediately, measured by the absence of detail-endpoint network requests while backgrounded.\n58\t- Given the detail endpoint is unavailable, then the job table degrades gracefully to showing only top-level state from the list endpoint and the existing 30-second list polling continues to function without regression.\n59\t- The odh-dashboard BFF proxy is verified to pass through all detail-endpoint response fields (including `status.benchmarks[]` and per-benchmark timestamps) without filtering.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- [P0] Auto-refresh mechanism for the Evaluations landing page job list — new detail-polling layer for in-progress job progress\n64\t- [P0] Non-blocking error handling during detail polling: last successful state preserved, inline warning, retry with exponential backoff\n65\t- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display — max-5 concurrent round-robin fetch for in-progress jobs on the current table page (fetching portion)\n66\t- [P1] Polling pauses when the browser tab is not in the foreground and resumes immediately on tab focus\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b54db860248c815f","agent_id":"a6c6a4f1b442ea14d","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"6eae1241-6b87-4c7f-93f3-6662d7770f71","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:10:10.025Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4139202dd638c4e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
