{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2deaf94b0cfe48e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E004\n3\ttitle: Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is only populated on completion, make\n16\t    elapsed time the primary progress indicator (earliest started_at, falling back\n17\t    to resource.created_at from the list endpoint) and show benchmark counts only\n18\t    for completed jobs.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDeliver the progress display for running evaluation jobs in the Evaluations landing page table, using the per-job detail data obtained through the detail-polling capability: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps. Elapsed time serves as the primary progress indicator for jobs with few benchmarks (a single-benchmark job shows only 0/N or N/N), with the benchmark count supplementary. Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Benchmark progress display: for a job with N benchmarks, render \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"` from the detail endpoint response.\n45\t- Elapsed time display: computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks, falling back to `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started; formatted for readability (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\").\n46\t- Initial-state behavior: until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, display only the top-level state from the list endpoint (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n47\t- Elapsed time as the primary progress indicator for single-benchmark/few-benchmark jobs, with benchmark count supplementary (mitigation for coarse progress granularity).\n48\t- UX/design review of the progress indicator pattern.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail endpoint response.\n53\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response (or `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started).\n54\t- Given no detail fetch has yet returned for a running job, then the row displays only the top-level state from the list endpoint, with no benchmark progress or elapsed time shown.\n55\t- Given a single-benchmark running job, then elapsed time is presented as the primary progress indicator for that row.\n56\t- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed and approved by UX/design.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- [P0] Auto-refresh mechanism for the Evaluations landing page job list — in-progress job progress made visible\n61\t- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` (display portion)\n62\t- [P1] Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b54db860248c815f","agent_id":"a6c6a4f1b442ea14d","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"49f5b549-7bc9-4286-9d2b-240d637060c4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:10:11.972Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2deaf94b0cfe48e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
