n the strategy (\"needs validation\" assumptions, Open Questions table) and each answer changes downstream scope with defined fallbacks. All three downstream epics that list E001 in `dependencies` set `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001`, and every `gated_by` target is in that epic's direct `dependencies` list. Every `gate_failure_impact` has both `action` (rewrite) and a substantive `fallback_approach` drawn from the strategy's own risk mitigations — these are true gates, not scheduling dependencies. E002's presence in E004's dependencies without `gated_by` is correct (build-against artifact, not an outcome gate). Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (hook, badge rendering, progress display).\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\nSignal fields are type-correct (E001 carries `investigation_signals`; E002-E004 carry `ai_signals`), all four ai-signals files exist, and rationales are substantive and cross-check against frontmatter values. E001's investigation signals are well-justified (question_specificity +1 for two enumerable questions; source_accessibility +1 for readable OSS server source; cluster_hardware_dependence -1 with the source-vs-empirical split explained). Two arguable values on E002: (a) `open_questions: 1` — the rationale (mechanics fully pinned by Staff Engineer Input) is defensible, but E002's own `gate_failure_impact` rewrites its scope if E001's answer is negative, and its siblings E003/E004 score the identical gate -1; the inconsistency makes this borderline rather than clearly correct. (b) `human_process_gates: 0` — E002 renders a user-facing PatternFly warning Alert, and the strategy lists UXD support as required, yet E003/E004 take -1 for the same UXD gate. Two arguable values in this criterion → 1 point. E003/E004 signal sets are consistent and well-justified (open_questions -1 tied to the specific gating question; human_process_gates -1 tied to UXD review ACs).\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nAll four epics have test