s are clean: E001 (AI Evaluations / TrustyAI / EvalHub — the server investigation subject) is separate from E002-E004 (AI Core Dashboard / ODH Dashboard). The passive odh-dashboard BFF component is correctly handled as an acceptance criterion on E002 rather than a padded epic. No scope duplication: E002 is the polling engine (hook, concurrency, retry, visibility), E003 is state badges from list-endpoint data, E004 is progress/elapsed display from detail data — three distinct work products on distinct data paths, not two epics rebuilding the same surface. The E002 vs E004 split along the engine/display axis is correct (E004 is not a thin increment on E002's surface — it is the consumer of a new hook's data). No work-product type mixing; each epic is comfortably within ~2 weeks for an S-sized strategy.\n44\t\n45\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n46\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: both questions are unresolved in the strategy (\"needs validation\" assumptions, Open Questions table) and each answer changes downstream scope with defined fallbacks. All three downstream epics that list E001 in `dependencies` set `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001`, and every `gated_by` target is in that epic's direct `dependencies` list. Every `gate_failure_impact` has both `action` (rewrite) and a substantive `fallback_approach` drawn from the strategy's own risk mitigations — these are true gates, not scheduling dependencies. E002's presence in E004's dependencies without `gated_by` is correct (build-against artifact, not an outcome gate). Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (hook, badge rendering, progress display).\n47\t\n48\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n49\tSignal fields are type-correct (E001 carries `investigation_signals`; E002-E004 carry `ai_signals`), all four ai-signals files exist, and rationales are substantive and cross-check against frontmatter values. E001's investigation signals are well-justified (question_specificity +1 for two enumerable questions; source_accessibility +1 for readable OSS server source; cluster_hardware_dependence -1 with the source-vs-empirical split explained). Two arguable values on E002: (a) `open_questions: 1` — the rationale (mechanics fully pinned by Staff Engineer Input) is defensible, but E002's own `gate_failure_impact` rewrites its scope if E001's answer is negative, and its siblings E003/E004 score the identical gate -1; the inconsistency makes this borderline rather than clearly correct. (b) `human_process_gates: 0` — E002 renders a user-facing PatternFly warning Alert, and the strategy lists UXD support as required, yet E003/E004 take -1 for the same UXD gate. Two arguable values in this criterion → 1 point. E003/E004 signal sets are consistent and well-justified (open_questions -1 tied to the specific gating question; human_process_gates -1 tied to UXD review ACs).\n50\t\n51\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n52\tAll four epics have testable ACs, most derived near-verbatim from the strategy's proposed ACs with measurable conditions (concurrency observed in dev tools, count matching `status.benchmarks[]` entries, elapsed-time formula, no network requests while backgrounded). No rule-mandated ACs apply — no replacement epic (nothing is replaced; the change is additive), no konflux-chain epic, no docs-authoring epic — so no rollback/doc-review/build-pipeline ACs are owed. No non-testable schedule-constraint ACs (the UXD-review ACs state an approvable outcome, not a timing constraint). No draft-ID references (\"E001\" etc.) appear in any epic body — epics reference each other only via full `RHAISTRAT-8005-ENNN` IDs or descriptive names.\n53\t\n54\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n55\tEvery strategy acceptance criterion maps to an epic AC (benchmark 3/5 progress → E004; 30s state-transition visibility → E003; elapsed time → E004; Queued distinction → E003; pre-start failure distinction → E003; error handling with retry → E002; tab-visibility pause → E002). All strategy capabilities