{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b59cf17cc58d801f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate EvalHub Server mid-run status data availability\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate EvalHub Server mid-run status data availability\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the two open questions from the strategy that gate the EvalHub UI progress-visibility work: (a) whether the EvalHub Server detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populates `status.benchmarks[]` with per-benchmark status entries while an evaluation job is still running, or only after completion; and (b) what values `status.message.message_code` takes for pre-start failures (admission errors, resource quota, scheduling failures) versus runtime failures, and whether those values are reliably distinguishable. The answers determine whether mid-run benchmark-level progress display and the pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction can be built as specified, or whether the defined fallbacks must be used.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source code (upstream `opendatahub-io/eval-hub`) status-reporting paths: where per-benchmark status entries, `started_at`/`completed_at` timestamps, and message codes are written, and whether they are updated during job execution (for example by a runtime watcher) or only at completion.\n34\t- Cross-check findings against the published API reference for `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}` and `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs`.\n35\t- Where feasible, confirm empirically by running an evaluation job against a development instance and inspecting detail-endpoint responses while the job is in progress.\n36\t- Enumerate the `message_code` values (or equivalent fields) emitted on admission/scheduling/resource-quota failure paths versus runtime failure paths, and assess whether the UI can reliably distinguish them.\n37\t- Publish the findings with a per-question go/no-go and the recommended fallback for each dependent UI feature (mid-run benchmark progress display; pre-start failure distinction).\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A documented answer, with evidence (source-code references and/or observed API responses), to whether `status.benchmarks[]` contains per-benchmark status entries while a job is running, or only after completion.\n42\t- A documented enumeration of `status.message.message_code` values for pre-start failure paths versus runtime failure paths, with a determination of whether they are reliably distinguishable.\n43\t- Findings delivered to the ODH Dashboard team with a clear go/no-go per dependent UI feature and a recommended fallback where the answer is negative.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs — de-risks feasibility of mid-run X/N progress and elapsed-time data\n48\t- [P1] Elapsed time display for running jobs — confirms availability of per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps mid-run\n49\t- [P2] Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction — determines whether `message_code` supports the distinction\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87740d0a423e0d67","agent_id":"a7ba9555a12ae6a06","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"9a4701af-9c2f-442c-806b-d2d83777a266","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:15:40.081Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b59cf17cc58d801f