{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bacb5adaf5270fd4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# RHAISTRAT-8005-E001 — Investigation Signals Rationale\n2\t\n3\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n4\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n5\t| question_specificity | +1 | Two concrete, enumerable questions with defined pass/fail criteria: (a) is `status.benchmarks[]` populated with per-benchmark status entries mid-run or only after completion; (b) which `message_code` values appear on pre-start failure paths vs. runtime failure paths. Both are stated in the strategy's Open Questions table. |\n6\t| source_accessibility | +1 | The EvalHub Server is an open-source Go repository (upstream `opendatahub-io/eval-hub`, mirrored at `red-hat-data-services/eval-hub`) with a published API reference; the status-reporting code paths that write `status.benchmarks[]` and message codes are readable source and determine the answer. An architecture context file (eval-hub.md) exists for the component. |\n7\t| local_runnability | 0 | The server binary can run locally (SQLite storage, local/development mode), but evaluation workloads are dispatched as Kubernetes batch Jobs via client-go, so empirically exercising a job mid-run requires a cluster rather than a plain downloaded binary/library. |\n8\t| cluster_hardware_dependence | -1 | The gating questions are answerable from readable server source and API docs (no cluster needed), but peripheral empirical confirmation — observing a detail-endpoint response while a job is actually running — requires a live cluster (development OpenShift/kind). No GPU or prod-scale hardware is required. |\n9\t| human_judgment_required | 0 | Both questions are technical fact-finding about observable server behavior; no stakeholder, product, or governance decision is needed to answer them. The strategy assigns ownership to the TrustyAI / EvalHub team, but resolution itself requires no human judgment call. |\n10\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87740d0a423e0d67","agent_id":"a7ba9555a12ae6a06","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"87ac984f-ad75-4497-a38e-ee249dcc82ab","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:15:45.966Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bacb5adaf5270fd4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
