{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a80511a147ea5d1d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# RHAISTRAT-8005-E002 — AI Signals Rationale\n2\t\n3\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n4\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n5\t| change_specificity | +1 | Staff Engineer Input fixes the design precisely: 10-second cycle, max-5 concurrent round-robin, visible-page-only targeting (client-side pagination, default 20 rows, options 5/10/20), retry constants (`RETRY_DELAY_MS * 2^attempt + jitter`, `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`), 4xx non-retryable, and the target endpoints. Existing files are named (`useEvaluationJobs.ts`, `k8s.ts`, `tablePaginationConstants.ts`). |\n6\t| pattern_precedent | +1 | The autorag and automl packages in the same odh-dashboard monorepo already use the React Query polling-with-retry pattern (`usePipelineRunQuery` in `packages/autorag/frontend/src/app/hooks/queries.ts`), and the existing 30s list polling in `useEvaluationJobs` is the layer this extends. |\n7\t| adapter_pattern | +1 | The epic explicitly replicates a cited reference implementation — the autorag `usePipelineRunQuery` pattern (placeholderData, exponential backoff, jitter) — per Staff Engineer direction. |\n8\t| existing_foundation | +1 | Extends the existing eval-hub-ui job list implementation (EvaluationsPage.tsx, useEvaluationJobs.ts, k8s.ts) and the existing BFF proxy path; no greenfield surface. |\n9\t| open_questions | -1 | This epic is gated on the same unresolved Investigation as its siblings: if `status.benchmarks[]` and per-benchmark timestamps turn out to be static while a job is running, this epic's own `gate_failure_impact` rewrites its scope (polling layer reduced to post-completion refresh, elapsed time sourced from the list endpoint). The mechanics (polling parameters, concurrency, retry, visibility) are fixed by Staff Engineer Input, but whether this epic is built as specified depends on an unresolved open question. |\n10\t| external_dependency | 0 | No upstream contribution or vendor coordination: both API endpoints exist, and PatternFly and React Query are already dependencies of the odh-dashboard monorepo. |\n11\t| human_process_gates | -1 | This epic renders a user-facing UI element — the non-blocking inline PatternFly warning Alert shown while status updates are temporarily unavailable — and the strategy lists UXD support as required (Pending human review). Consistent with the sibling UI epics, a human design review gates completion of this deliverable. The pending Performance Team review of polling load remains advisory (the Staff Engineer deferred scalability for this release) and is not the basis for this score. |\n12\t| repo_access | +1 | The odh-dashboard repository is public (`opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard`); the eval-hub-ui plugin code is directly accessible and modifiable. |\n13\t| architecture_claims | +1 | The strategy cites specific architecture context (odh-dashboard.md for the Module Federation/BFF proxy chain, eval-hub.md for the auth model and cache TTLs backing the polling-load claim), and both files exist in `.context/architecture-context/`. |\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87740d0a423e0d67","agent_id":"a7ba9555a12ae6a06","session_id":"2253a725-5f5e-46df-9ff1-988eb7749e1b","uuid":"b8bd4f1d-d800-45e0-a456-d8dfcf19ceb7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:15:46.726Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a80511a147ea5d1d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
